From 11640a3219d3370352f51928a83003aa6cd665b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PocketForge CI <ci@pocketforge.local>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 08:45:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 30/30] tests: cover A133 BootROM eGON load and SRAM reset

Add the pocketforge-a133-bootrom qtest: a forged eGON.BT0 SPL fixture
boots from MMC0 at the 8 KiB and 128 KiB locations with an exact-length
copy into SRAM A1, the boot-media stamp, AArch32 entry at 0x20000 and
held secondaries, and stale-checksum, bad-magic, bad-length,
truncated-media and no-media fixtures must be rejected without any copy
or execution. Wired into tests/qtest/meson.build; build.sh picks the
patch up in the same change.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 tests/qtest/meson.build                     |    3 
 tests/qtest/pocketforge-a133-bootrom-test.c |  414 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 416 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

